l_weight += mr\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\n                break\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected, cannot form MST\")\n    return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}\n```\n\nCheck that distances list includes all pairs? Not required but if not, MST may be disconnected.\n\nNow produce JSON with escaped source. In Python, we can use json.dumps to escape. But the response must be the JSON directly. I'll write the implementation as a string with proper escaping.\n\nSince the output is a single JSON object with key \"implementation\", I can construct as:\n\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    core = case[\\\"core_distance\\\"]\\n    dists = case[\\\"distances\\\"]\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n not in core:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing core distance for node {n}\\\")\\n    edges = []\\n    for a, b, d in dists:\\n        if a == b:\\n            continue\\n        mr = max(core[a], core[b], d)\\n        if a > b:\\n            a, b = b, a\\n        edges.append((mr, a, b))\\n    edges.sort()\\n    parent = {n: n for n in nodes}\\n    rank = {n: 0 for n in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for mr, a, b in edges:\\n        if union(a, b):\\n            mst_edges.append([a, b, mr])\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    if len(mst_e